{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1002929-apartment-complexes-and-gated-communitys-how-do-supernaturals-fit-in","id":1002929,"title":"Apartment complexes and Gated Communitys, how do supernaturals fit in","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-14T09:43:49-08:00","id":1002929,"title":"Apartment complexes and Gated Communitys, how do supernaturals fit in","content":"Garou have the curse, Vampires are strictly nocturnal, Mages and changelings, both come accross as ... idiocyntric.<br /> <br /> Vampires can cut through the problem somewhat by employing a ghoul to hold tenancy, any other ideas","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T10:16:29-08:00","id":1002941,"title":"","content":"Are we talking about living there, or just visiting? There are tribes of Garou who live in cities and by extension, the sort of places you are describing. I think Glass Walkers as well as some of the less-poor Gnawers might have apartments. Werewolves would probably make for fearful neighbors, but at least they might keep some of the worst aspects of urban blight at bay. Gates and walls don't do much to stop determined shifters, if they need to circumvent security measures.<br /> <br /> What problem would a vampire have in living in an apartment, specifically? Why would they need a ghoul? I just don't see tenements as some sort of hyper-secure bastion that most supernaturals would have to worry about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T10:52:41-08:00","id":1002962,"title":"","content":"I think that Kindred would prefer gated communities to apartment complexes. Their ghouls would inhabit the house while they would inhabit the basement. I think that they would have a hidden room within the basement where the Kindred could sleep in safety, perhaps guarded by a few ghoul dogs who would sleep in the basement during the day. While they would have to spend six blood points per month to maintain their ghouls, I think that most Kindred would find the ghouls are worthwhile investment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T11:37:19-08:00","id":1002982,"title":"","content":"From experience low rent apartment complexes would not be ideal. Many is the tale I've heard of uninvited intrusions from management. Add to that thin walls, security patrols and dozens of witnesses to your comings and goings. If it was more up-market and you or an ally had some degree of control that'd be something better but you'd need to be able to manipulate or trust or manipulate security and maintenance at the bare minimum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5445-elizabethsterling","name":"ElizabethSterling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5445_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T12:32:56-08:00","id":1003011,"title":"","content":"if your too poor to afford something upscale is a makeshift place better then a low rent apartment complex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T15:07:20-08:00","id":1003091,"title":"","content":"I think a cheap tenement would be an excellent place for a lair if one discards the convention of living like a human being and thinks like a predator. That crawlspace that the heating ducts run through or the unused broom closet next to the basement laundry room that management lost the key to provide excellent hiding places to sit out the day, and during the night those paper-thin walls will have desensitized residents to screams and the sounds of struggle. A virtual buffet for the vampire who doesn't mind getting his hands dirty!<br /> <br /> As for gated communities, well...<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zW3j4aFg9xU\" data-code=\"zW3j4aFg9xU\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/zW3j4aFg9xU/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T18:22:26-08:00","id":1003183,"title":"","content":"Hm, I have never lived in an apartment complex with crawlspaces that large (radiators or central heating).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T13:57:08-08:00","id":1004612,"title":"","content":"Mine has an above-ceiling crawlspace just under a meter high. Had me worried when frat boys were doing parkour off a neighboring building onto our roof. (Though not as worried as they should have been given how badly they scared my crazy gun-waving single mom neighbor. Could have easily gone from ATO or PKA to DOA...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T14:46:13-08:00","id":1004645,"title":"","content":"ideas what a Garou can do about the curse, in a apt complex, everyone can tell hes &quot;Creepy&quot;<br /> <br /> In a gated community he might be dissmised as a recluse... if he keeps to himself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=